    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T20:17:04Z",
    "body": "Stopped at Step 5. This host has only the x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu Rust target. Wine is not installed.\n\nUpstream main e808c9629 still calls the stderr logging initializer after the Windows console attachment. It has no file fallback. This is not evidence that the issue is fixed.\n\nI wrote nine proposed portable tests for the path selection, stderr handle selection, and bounded file writer. I tried to compile them with rustc. Compilation failed because the proposed gui_log module does not exist. No test ran. This failure does not reproduce the existing Windows behavior.\n\nI cannot establish the required failing behavioral test on unchanged code on this host. I made no production changes and opened no PR. PR #2239 changes the logging initializer. A future fix that changes that initializer must stack on #2239.\n\nClaim released. The issue is free again. The failed compilation output and proposed tests remain in /tmp on len. They are not committed.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
