    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T10:44:13Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main b629dc7e8 for the missing desktop log. Source inspection shows that commit 66633a80c adds the file logger for #2421.\n\nThe desktop entry point calls logging::init_desktop after Windows console attachment. The initializer writes tracing events to camcraft.log in the per-user configuration directory. It also keeps the stderr subscriber. Windows failure dialogs call logging::failure_message, which names the log path.\n\nEvidence: crates/ui/src/main.rs, crates/app/src/logging_desktop.rs, and crates/ui/src/win_console.rs. Existing tests in crates/ui/tests/startup_log.rs cover startup errors, file persistence, prior-run retention, and panic diagnostics. I inspected these tests. I did not run them or a Windows executable.\n\nOne requirement remains absent: the file has no size cap or rotation. The decision note docs/decisions/2421-startup-log-uma.md explicitly leaves retention limits for later work. This evidence does not establish that every acceptance condition of #1323 is complete.\n\nSuggest closing the original missing-log report if #2421 supersedes it; the maintainer decides. Keep the retention requirement open if it is still required. I made no source changes and did not claim the issue.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
